title: Cameras - 50/50 Split View in Camera Menu Enable
raw_community_title: Enable 50/50 view in camera menu
category: Cameras and ADAS
platform: F-150 Lightning
model_years: 2022-2023
trim: All
validated: true
verified_by: Kyle / AsBuiltPro & Lightning Community
source_sheet: F-150 Lightning FORScan Thread
notes: Adds a button to Sync camera selection screen that shows a 50/50 view of the
  two side cameras. Standard on 2024+.
steps:
- module: APIM
  address: 7D0-01-01
  mask: xxxx *xxx xx--
  nibbles:
  - nibble: 4
    community_instruction: if 1 change to 3
    bits:
    - bit: 3
      action: 0
      feature_name: Brazil Frequency (BF)
      target_state: Disabled
    - bit: 2
      action: 0
      feature_name: Cross Traffic Braking (CTB)
      target_state: Disabled
    - bit: 1
      action: 0
      feature_name: 50/50 Views (V)
      target_state: Disabled
    - bit: 0
      action: 0
      feature_name: Locking Differential (LD)
      target_state: Disabled
- module: APIM
  address: 7D0-01-04
  mask: xxxx xxxx x*--
  nibbles:
  - nibble: 9
    community_instruction: if 0 change to 1, if 8 change to 9
    bits:
    - bit: 3
      action: 0
      feature_name: Smart Hitch (SH)
      target_state: Disabled
    - bit: 2
      action: 0
      feature_name: Cross Traffic/Emergency Braking with Split View (CTEBSV)
      target_state: Disabled
    - bit: 1
      action: 0
      feature_name: Zone Lighting - Power Roller Shutter (ZLPRS)
      target_state: Disabled
    - bit: 0
      action: 0
      feature_name: 50/50 View at Speed (VS)
      target_state: Disabled
validation_status: validated
